            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157257453?u=7cc52be502cc0610711673156efccd05cfbd05a3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Is there an existing issue for this?</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have searched the existing issues</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Current Behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On <a href=\"https://npmjs.com/settings/your-username/packages\" rel=\"nofollow\">your profile's package page</a>, there seems to be a grammar issue if you only have 1 package:</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/157257453/469252576-1ab29a86-d811-4b16-abe4-9be5da7a14f1.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzE5Njc1NDUsIm5iZiI6MTc3MTk2NzI0NSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNTcyNTc0NTMvNDY5MjUyNTc2LTFhYjI5YTg2LWQ4MTEtNGIxNi1hYmU0LTliZTVkYTdhMTRmMS5wbmc_.oLiwawRz9-tel2rn7balyOwRFrqP3V08vLZ_tJ6rWjg\"><img width=\"1440\" height=\"710\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/157257453/469252576-1ab29a86-d811-4b16-abe4-9be5da7a14f1.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzE5Njc1NDUsIm5iZiI6MTc3MTk2NzI0NSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNTcyNTc0NTMvNDY5MjUyNTc2LTFhYjI5YTg2LWQ4MTEtNGIxNi1hYmU0LTliZTVkYTdhMTRmMS5wbmc_.oLiwawRz9-tel2rn7balyOwRFrqP3V08vLZ_tJ6rWjg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 710px;\"></a>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected Behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If the user only has one package, it should say '1 package' instead of '1 packages'.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps To Reproduce</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What is this section for? I don't understand.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Environment</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>npm: Latest, but doesn't matter</li>\n<li>Node: Latest, but doesn't matter</li>\n<li>OS: MacOS 15.??, but this isn't related to OS</li>\n<li>platform: MacBook Pro, but that shouldn't matter either</li>\n</ul>",
